<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Battle of Panipat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1556</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Battle of Panipat was fought on 5 November 1556 north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> between the young Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, under his regent Bairam Khan, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hemu">Hemu</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> general who had taken Delhi for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sur-empire">Sur dynasty</a>. Hemu had the upper hand until an arrow struck him in the eye; his army broke, and he was captured and killed. The victory restored Mughal rule in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-panipat.jpg" alt="Second Battle of Panipat" width="320" height="530" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kankar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_defeat_of_Hemu,_Akbarnama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
